--- !u!114 &428905344
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 428905342}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "I find myself at a loss for words, though I certainly have no shortage
    of thoughts on the matter. It is with growing frustration that I write this letter,
    the contents of which I should have addressed long ago. It appears I was far
    too hasty in trusting you with a deal that, in hindsight, has proven to be nothing
    short of a disaster.\n\nWhat I had anticipated as a mutually beneficial arrangement
    has, instead, left me with nothing but regret. The terms\u2014vague at best and
    misleading at worst\u2014have done nothing but complicate matters and harm my
    interests. You assured me that the deal would yield favorable results, but I
    am now left wondering if I was the only one who failed to see the obvious flaws
    from the outset. The lack of transparency is infuriating, and your disregard
    for my expectations is, frankly, insulting.\n\nI had hoped for a professional,
    courteous exchange, but it seems that is far too much to expect from someone
    of your caliber. I demand an explanation for this fiasco, and I trust it will
    be offered without delay. At this point, my patience is exhausted, and my tolerance
    for further incompetence is thin.\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_fontSharedMaterials: []
  m_fontMaterial: {fileID: 0}
  m_fontMaterials: []
  m_fontColor32:
